{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_17f42bdf6dd199f2bac8c4854c7b0ea429cc7379cc40dc8e238387c1ae99fab4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_41fc0927b9e9fc09166fcd86bef0b65b0c1e2a3efa0d35752d346ec3d1223fd9","slc_bb7dba530a050f69c5943efcdb46053670973a71eea46ebe86a9b0d0a65ba95e"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"RepoAgent provides a CLI: 'repoagent run' generates or updates docs, 'repoagent clean' removes repoagent-related cache, and 'repoagent diff' previews which docs would be updated or generated from current code changes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_26cde967f1253d87580c97250ec6598703127fe9b981655ed2fdb1256a1d93fa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3a390b1d149c7658a60c3c7d7e2b050ac16c6bcf260d563abcdd29d056c152d8"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"Per its README features, RepoAgent detects Git changes (additions, deletions, modifications), analyzes code structure via AST to document individual objects, and identifies bidirectional inter-object invocation relationships.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_28d14f54703e22b6494602c0cf978c2dced9bcb7e2dc9d5c5c3156f8431f738e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8c0b6717facac41863623f0e9114f09117d993bae81b021e75d9e3367e83c6b5","slc_f1046641a0263e66927716c02b05d3775471200189deb0c1f1d7e30101b0c1bd"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"The pre-commit hook example notes that currently only Python is supported as a trigger file type, and the roadmap lists multi-language support (Java, C, C++) as an unchecked future-work item.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6c1ec0a384781c6f1b2b87441c20cefd66f9e63d89b71add4f1cf4820af0c063","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_da75808be421d6efacaaf57b38c8dc29684e2a4455982aabc181c125f4e9db5c","slc_ecd3ff750a7ac298ced402ccc03cfbc040cdbc730ebccf2538a83cb800291ac7"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"Chat With Repo is described as a preliminary prototype of one downstream task, with adapting its interface to various downstream applications left as future research.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b02934ac18746567547c49cf12f35c75324f25be301a20d80a8ffe6eae5ab99","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_28c9a6120db898a62a7985b5e22b81d18d4b0db8361cb3d6c8176b43b0f8b9bb","slc_38cf6a95d4f3b40209f19c54183ee2d65bc5a89f78e762c5fa7d528d5eaf5618","slc_f1046641a0263e66927716c02b05d3775471200189deb0c1f1d7e30101b0c1bd"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"In a target git repository, users can configure a pre-commit hook (entry: repoagent, types: [python]) so each git commit triggers automatic change detection and document generation, with RepoAgent modifying staged files before the commit completes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9cde1d58094281c30426472923de3f14fd78887cfd46896d9ce250eef9936a10","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_16271ee0b9fe8cced86cd12df853cda2a0a2f04f6bc913df0a56d03377bcf0ef","slc_dba6be21ea75c32884e1ec203dee80896c9251febd68d928a0a72b3935061aaf"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"The run command accepts optional flags overriding config defaults, including --model (default gpt-3.5-turbo), --temperature (0.2), --request-timeout (60), --base-url, --target-repo-path, --hierarchy-path, --markdown-docs-path, --ignore-list, --language (default Chinese), and --log-level.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","created_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9f53fd5febb995b8e9c38be65c25e87985f124c366112bb4820603859b99288d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"openbmb/repoagent@825d988127d7 snapshot eea8cc889eeddaae","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10b3ae90ec0edf52df032d49e6c2c8d662ca74d744ad980806172a8e9624dd81","slc_b02935f5f520064d4ff29b5788c9fe417440b8d751a8c4f80c0b268bae525ed9"],"source_ids":["src_e9d8cac110365200898afedd0e533306"],"text":"Before configuring parameters, the OpenAI API key must be set as an environment variable, with instructions given for Linux/Mac, Windows cmd, and PowerShell.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:14:14Z","updated_by_operation":"op_13ecda92f13b4590a5767c6d36298dc3"}
